course: dictionary
lesson: 16092
title: A watercourse is a channel for water
level: primary-5
stars: 0
explain: A watercourse is any channel that water flows along. A river, a stream, a brook, a ditch and a canal are all watercourses, big or small. «The rain ran off the hill into the watercourse and down to the sea.»
explain: Look at the two parts of the word: water and course. The course is the path the water takes as it moves. If you can see water moving along a channel, you are looking at a watercourse.
explain: Maps show watercourses as blue lines, so you can spot them on a map. Geography lessons use the word when they study rivers and the water cycle. «Pollution of watercourses harms fish, and it is against the law.»
fact: A watercourse is any channel that water flows along.
fact: Rivers, streams, brooks, ditches and canals are all watercourses.
fact: «A natural watercourse» is one made by nature, such as a river, rather than by people.
fact: Maps show watercourses as blue lines.
fact: Polluting a watercourse harms fish and is against the law.
exercise: «The rain ran down the hill into the watercourse.» What is a watercourse? | * A channel that water flows along | A type of rain cloud | A stone wall by a field | A hill covered in grass
exercise: «Ben walked along the watercourse to look for ducks.» Where was Ben walking? | Inside a shop | * Beside a channel of flowing water | On top of a mountain | Under a bridge with no water at all
exercise: Which of these is a watercourse? | * A canal | A school bag | A tall tree | A bus stop
test: Ella says, «The brook is a watercourse because water flows along it.» Why is she right? | Brooks are only puddles in the garden | * Water flows along the brook, so it is a channel for water | Brooks are always made of stone | A brook is a kind of bird
test: On a map, what do the blue lines usually show? | Roads for buses | * Watercourses, like rivers and streams | Mountains and hills | Parks and gardens
exam: Why is it harmful to pollute a watercourse? | It makes the rivers wider | It turns the water into rain | * It harms fish and is against the law | It makes the grass grow taller
